Annoyingly clever. Even while running Ito JavaScript I have to debate whether I should be annoyingly clever or not.<p><pre><code>  /* bad use of while loop with compound if-statement */
  while ((len = getline(line, MAXLINE)) > 0)
    if (len > max) {
        max = len;
        copy(longest, line);
    }
 if (max > 0) /* there was a line */
    printf("%s", longest);
</code></pre>
What do you do?
